                    <msContents><!-- describe the intellectual content of an inscription -->
                        <summary>This inscription records the gift of an agrahāra by Rēvarasa, who was ruling the region of Medaku-300 from Ravipoḷ. In the Pramādi samvatsara, he renewed a previous grant made by Saṁkaragaṇḍa to the brāhman Pāmbalapāla Veṇṇayya in the Vr̥ṣabha samvatsara. 
                            The inscription provides details of the donation and lists the witnesses and the executors, including the eight lords (prabhū), and one hundred mahājana.  </summary>
                        <!-- offers the possibility to give a summary of the inscription's content -->
                    </msContents>
